# The negative half of issue #830. The `(` path must reach the Heritage `value-of-reader` only
# when the reader is actually there — `value` heads it (`spec/grammar.md:217`) solely when `of`
# directly follows. Parenthesizing a bare `value` must NOT smuggle the keyword in as a
# `parenthesized-call` callee (`spec/grammar.md:215`); it stays rejected exactly as it is in any
# other expression position (#853, #885).
#
# This shape had no conformance coverage at all before this fixture: the one fixture asserting
# `ol-bad-token` on a bare `value`, `core-language/diagnostics/reserved-word-in-value-position`,
# covers the UNparenthesized position only — proven by it staying GREEN under the mutation that
# makes `isCalleeName` accept `value`, which is precisely the mutation that reopens #830.
#
# Heritage + Data are active so this asserts the rejection under the same profile set as the
# positive twin, where the reader IS available (`spec/conformance.md:305`).
print (value)
